      "content": "Preemptive strikes to prevent authoritarian rise are not inherently justifiable under traditional democratic realism, as WTO law and the UN Charter generally require an imminent threat to authorize such force. Most moral frameworks prioritize the evils of war and promote diplomatic engagement as the superior, less coercive alternative to military action. Therefore, a definitive moral framework would strictly limit such strikes to cases of indisputable, immediate preventable harm that cannot averted by any non-forceful means.",
